# Mechanical Chicken from An OOX of Your Own: rescue Oglethorpe Obnoticus's
# three homing robots, then visit him in Booty Bay.
# Sources: quests.json (the OOX chain, its givers and turn-ins, levels); the
# world database (An OOX of Your Own rewards item 10398; the beacons' droppers
# and rates, Classic drop data); Forever's client data (the beacons need level
# 40 and 43); the knowledge base's quest notes (ambushes, robot positions).

step OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon in Feralas
  tip Each robot starts with a distress beacon that mobs in its zone drop, about one kill in 40 to 100 in Classic's data. In Feralas the best are the Coast Crawl Snapclaws and Deepseers (levels 43-45) on the Forgotten Coast and the Sprite Dragons (47-48), about 2.5%; ogres, harpies, naga and Grimtotems drop it about 1%. You can loot it from level 40.
  collect 8705 x1 nearest

step Rescue OOX-22/FE
  tip Right-click the beacon. OOX-22/FE sits in a cave near Feral Scar Vale, among yetis and apes. Its escort runs west along the road to the dock on the Forgotten Coast with three ambushes: three yetis, then three gorillas, then four or five gnolls with a caster. Bring a friend if you are under 47. The robot keeps walking unless it is hit, so stay close; if it will not move, another player has it: wait for it to come back. Its turn-in is in Booty Bay; keep the quest for later.
  accept 2766
  turnin 2766
  accept 2767
  complete 2767                       -- Escort OOX-22/FE

step OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon in Tanaris
  zone Tanaris
  tip Tanaris mobs drop OOX-17/TN's beacon about one kill in 50 to 150. Best: the Treasure Hunting Pirates and Buccaneers on the south shore (44-45) and the Ground Pounders in the north (41-43), about 2%. You can loot it from level 43.
  collect 8623 x1 nearest

step Rescue OOX-17/TN
  zone Tanaris
  tip OOX-17/TN stands in the hills near the Gaping Chasm in south-east Tanaris. Its escort to Steamwheedle Port has two ambushes: three scorpids near the start, three Wastewander bandits near the end. The robot has about 3,000 health and stops to fight what you attack, so it can tank for a moment while you recover. Its turn-in is in Booty Bay too.
  accept 351
  turnin 351
  accept 648
  complete 648                        -- Escort OOX-17/TN

step OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon in the Hinterlands
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip Most Hinterlands mobs drop OOX-09/HL's beacon about once in 100 kills: Silvermane wolves, owlbeasts, Highvale elves, Witherbark and Vilebranch trolls. You can loot it from level 43.
  collect 8704 x1 nearest

step Rescue OOX-09/HL
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip OOX-09/HL waits on the largest island of the lake west of Skulk Rock. Its escort to the shore beyond Overlook Cliff has two ambushes of three: Marauding Owlbeasts, then Vilebranch Ambushers; the robot warns you just before each.
  accept 485
  turnin 485
  accept 836
  complete 836                        -- Escort OOX-09/HL

step Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Oglethorpe Obnoticus is in Booty Bay, upstairs in the building north of the inn, above First Mate Crazz. Hand in all three rescues; at level 45 he then offers An OOX of Your Own, which you turn straight back in for the Mechanical Chicken.
  turnin 2767
  turnin 648
  turnin 836
  level 45
  accept 3721
  turnin 3721
  collect 10398 @28.4,76.4            -- Mechanical Chicken
